---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
const lastUpdated = "2026-04-28";
---
<Base title="terms — velocit.ee" description="Terms of use for velocit.ee — the marketing site, the waitlist, and the contact form.">
  <article>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-wrap px-6 lg:px-10 py-16">
      <p class="label">// legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-mono text-4xl text-cream tracking-tightest">terms of use</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-2xs font-mono text-muted">last updated · {lastUpdated}</p>

      <section class="mt-10 prose">
        <p>
          These terms apply to <strong>velocit.ee</strong> — this website, the waitlist, and the
          contact form. They <em>do not</em> apply to the engines themselves; those are open
          source under <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0">Apache 2.0</a>, governed by
          the licence text you'll find in
          <a href="https://github.com/velocit-ee/core/blob/main/LICENSE">velocit-ee/core/LICENSE</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>Don't:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the waitlist or contact form to send unsolicited content to other addresses.</li>
          <li>Attempt to break things — denial of service, exploiting unpatched bugs, etc. If you find a security issue, please email <a href="mailto:security@velocit.ee">security@velocit.ee</a> and we will respond rapidly.</li>
          <li>Pretend to be us, or use the velocit.ee name/marks in a way that suggests affiliation we haven't agreed to.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The site is provided as-is. We're a small team; we don't guarantee uptime; if velocit.ee is
          down when you visit, refresh in five minutes. The engines come with the warranty disclaimers
          stated in the Apache 2.0 licence itself (sections 7 and 8).
        </p>

        <h2>Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent permitted by EU/German law, velocit.ee is not liable for indirect or consequential
          damages arising from your use of this site or the engines. The licence governs the engines; this
          governs the site.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms. Material changes will be announced via the blog and on the org GitHub.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:legal@velocit.ee">legal@velocit.ee</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
